<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Winbel half year EPS rises, no div.</title>
<headline>Winbel half year EPS rises, no div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended March 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - attrib		  4.6	   vs 3.1</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   2.46	  vs 1.61</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   5.54	  vs 4.68</p>
<p>    Tax			 0.54	  vs 0.84</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   1.33	  vs 1.06</p>
<p>    Turnover		  157.87	vs 130.87</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     0.15	  vs nil</p>
<p>Full name: Winbel Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said no interim dividend had been declared. Shareholders were directed to a cautionary dated June 13 concerning talks with outside shareholders. Directors said that if talks were successful they would have a material stabilising effect on group company Inmins Ltd. The effect on the earnings per share of Imnins, Winhold Ltd and Winbel was not ascertainable until negotiations were finalised.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
